WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.606
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:16.517
Unit thirty-five: Adverbs of Degree (very / quite / really). Today you will show how strong an adjective or verb is.

4
00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:19.539
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.023
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.652
Very.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.487
Very means to a high degree.

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:30.270
It is very hot.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.362
Your turn. Say: Very.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:36.888
Very.

11
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.500
Quite.

12
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:41.597
Quite means to a fairly high degree.

13
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:43.777
The film was quite long.

14
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:47.024
Your turn. Say: Quite.

15
00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:50.612
Quite.

16
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.212
Really.

17
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:55.739
Really means truly; very much.

18
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.734
I am really tired.

19
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.631
Your turn. Say: Really.

20
00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:04.305
Really.

21
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.190
Extremely.

22
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:09.810
Extremely means to a very high degree.

23
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:12.091
It is extremely cold.

24
00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:15.220
Your turn. Say: Extremely.

25
00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.219
Extremely.

26
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:20.775
A bit.

27
00:01:21.783 --> 00:01:23.133
A bit means a little.

28
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.159
The soup is a bit hot.

29
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.182
Your turn. Say: A bit.

30
00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:31.872
A bit.

31
00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:33.293
Too.

32
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:35.807
Too means more than is good.

33
00:01:36.417 --> 00:01:37.754
It is too noisy.

34
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.526
Your turn. Say: Too.

35
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.019
Too.

36
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:45.587
Enough.

37
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:48.455
Enough means as much as is needed.

38
00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.341
It is warm enough.

39
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.219
Your turn. Say: Enough.

40
00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:56.743
Enough.

41
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.508
Completely.

42
00:01:59.517 --> 00:02:01.493
Completely means in every way.

43
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.816
I am completely lost.

44
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:07.232
Your turn. Say: Completely.

45
00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.010
Completely.

46
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.393
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.029
Visal, how was the film? Use an adverb of degree.

48
00:02:21.117 --> 00:02:32.500
It was quite long, but really interesting. Adverbs of degree tell us how strong an adjective is: a bit, quite, very, really, extremely.

49
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:34.828
Where do they go?

50
00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:48.356
Before the adjective or another adverb: very hot, quite slowly, extremely difficult. Too and enough also show degree: too hot means more than good; hot enough means sufficient.

51
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:50.834
Any traps?

52
00:02:51.950 --> 00:03:04.430
Do not use very with extreme adjectives. We say absolutely amazing, not very amazing. Use completely with words like lost or wrong. Choose the degree that matches your feeling.

53
00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.183
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.017 --> 00:03:12.106
Grammar focus: Adverbs of degree: adverb plus adjective.

55
00:03:12.406 --> 00:03:13.697
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:15.965
The film was quite long.

57
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.257
I am really tired.

58
00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.277
The exam was extremely difficult.

59
00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:32.562
Put a bit, quite, very, really and extremely before an adjective or adverb. Too means more than good; enough means sufficient. Use absolutely with extreme adjectives.

60
00:03:33.317 --> 00:03:36.712
Be careful! Don't say: It is very absolutely good.

61
00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.585
Say: It is absolutely good.

62
00:03:40.885 --> 00:03:42.710
Do not use two degree words.

63
00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.955
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:47.872
How Strong?.

65
00:03:48.172 --> 00:03:49.928
The weather is very hot today.

66
00:03:50.933 --> 00:03:53.525
The film was quite long, but it was really interesting.

67
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.705
I am a bit tired, but I am not completely exhausted.

68
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.734
The exam was extremely difficult.

69
00:04:01.733 --> 00:04:04.917
The soup is too hot, and the room is not warm enough.

70
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:10.174
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.750
The soup is blank hot. I can't eat it.

72
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:17.518
A, too. B, enough. C, a bit very.

73
00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.846
The answer is A: too.

74
00:04:23.983 --> 00:04:26.473
I am blank tired. (very strong)

75
00:04:26.773 --> 00:04:30.450
A, extremely. B, a bit. C, enough.

76
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.023
The answer is A: extremely.

77
00:04:37.183 --> 00:04:38.823
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:39.123 --> 00:04:44.750
A, It is very amazing.. B, It is very good.. C, It is very absolutely good..

79
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.903
The answer is B: It is very good..

80
00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:55.004
The film was blank long, but fine. (fairly)

81
00:04:55.304 --> 00:04:58.876
A, quite. B, extremely. C, completely.

82
00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:04.073
The answer is A: quite.

83
00:05:05.217 --> 00:05:07.808
According to the reading, how was the exam?

84
00:05:08.108 --> 00:05:12.946
A, extremely difficult. B, a bit easy. C, quite short.

85
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.277
The answer is A: extremely difficult.

86
00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:23.525
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:24.383 --> 00:05:26.987
Describe your day with two adverbs of degree.

88
00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:37.458
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:37.758 --> 00:05:52.441
My day was quite busy and really interesting. I was a bit tired in the evening, but I was very happy. I use adverbs of degree such as quite, really, a bit and very to show how strong my feelings were.

90
00:05:52.741 --> 00:05:54.636
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:55.550 --> 00:06:01.012
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adverbs of degree: adverb plus adjective.

92
00:06:01.312 --> 00:06:05.230
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.321
See you in Unit thirty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.621 --> 00:06:11.111
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

